
---
import DocsLayout from '/src/layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import DocsCode from '/src/components/DocsCode.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Lua & LSL Docs">
<div class="dashboard summary-function">
  <div class="dashboard-header">
    <span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll.Die()`} lang="slua" /></span>
    <span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`llDie();`} lang="lsl" /></span>
  </div>

  <div class="dashboard-body">
    <div class="dash-col">
      <p>  <p>Deletes the object. The object does <b>not</b> go to the owner's Inventory <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Trash" target="_blank">🗑 Trash</a>.</p>
  <p>If called in any prim in the <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Link_set" target="_blank">link set</a> the result will be the deletion of the entire object.</p>
  <p>To remove a single prim from an object, use <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlBreakLink" target="_blank">llBreakLink</a> first.</p>
</p>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Categories</div>
      <ul class="meta-list">
        <li>rez</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Tech Specs</div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">LSO ID</span><span class="tech-val">41</span></div>

      <div class="label-stack">
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
  <h2>Caveats</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The script may not stop executing immediately after this function is called (<a href="https://jira.secondlife.com/browse/SVC-7421" target="_blank">SVC-7421</a>).</li>
    <li>After this function is called, there is no way to undo the deletion of the object.</li>
    <li>Has no effect if called from within an <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Category:LSL_Attachment" target="_blank">attachment</a>; there is no way to delete an attachment.
    <ul>
      <li>To detach an object from the avatar, call <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlDetachFromAvatar" target="_blank">llDetachFromAvatar</a>.</li>
      <li><a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlDetachFromAvatar" target="_blank">Detaching</a> a <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlAttachToAvatarTemp" target="_blank">temporary attachment</a> will cause the attachment to be deleted.</li>
    </ul>
  
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Useful Snippets</h2>
  <p><a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlRemoveInventory" target="_blank">llRemoveInventory</a> of <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlGetScriptName" target="_blank">llGetScriptName</a> deletes just the calling script, rather than all of the objects that the calling script contains. For instance, you can write a script that chats a little when dragged onto an object from inventory and then politely disappears itself, such as:</p>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`-- http://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/llDie
local function main()
    ll.OwnerSay("llGetRegionTimeDilation()")
    ll.OwnerSay(tostring(ll.GetRegionTimeDilation()))
    ll.RemoveInventory(ll.GetScriptName())
end

main()
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`// http://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/llDie
default
{
    state_entry()
    {
        llOwnerSay("llGetRegionTimeDilation()");
        llOwnerSay((string) llGetRegionTimeDilation());
        llRemoveInventory(llGetScriptName());
    }
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
